A||||3||Raydar||88 V-6 EGR tube and headlight questions.||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||05-07-2001||12:17 AM||||1. Is the EGR tube on the 88 V-6 the same as the ones on the 85-87? I got a used one from one of the local guys and installed it, but it seemed like it was about 3/8" too short. Finally got it to flex enough to connect, but it seemed like it really didn't want to. Not going to be surprised if it breaks again. <P>2. In order to get my headlights to come up, I either have to turn on the parking lights first, then the headlights. Or turn them on, off and on again, quickly. I'm guessing either the module or the switch. Anybody have any experience with this? (87 and 88 style.)<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-07-2001||12:54 AM||||I take it, from your signature, that you went through with the trade for your T-Topper.  I hope it all worked out OK.<P>As far as your headlight problem......it could be either the switch or the module.  Obviously I would try the switch first.  If that doesn't do it then the module might be messed up.  LMK.....I have a few spare modules (and switches) lying around.  I even have one or two new switches.<P>I almost forgot about the EGR tube......yes, the '88 tubes are different than the '85-'87s.  You can interchange them, like you did, by carefully bending it to fit, but it would be better to get the "proper" one. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 05-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou_dias||05-07-2001||02:32 AM||||I just blocked mine off at the intake and at the EGR tube and all of a sudden my car runs like it has 20 extra horses...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-07-2001||09:33 AM||||Thanks for your responses.<BR>Yes, we did the trade. I hope Ronnie and Carolyn are as satisfied as I am.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'll try swapping switches and or modules. Hopefully the ones on my parts car are undamaged. <BR>As for blocking off the EGR, I've heard bad things about it. Burned pistons and such.<BR>I also have to pass smog tests every year, so that's not really an option. Thanks, tho'!  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
